---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import Face from '../components/Face.astro'
import Logo from '../components/Logo.astro'
import DownloadList from '../components/DownloadList.astro'
import { loadDownloads } from '../lib/downloads'

const downloads = await loadDownloads()
const github = 'https://github.com/The1UNeed/hexbot'

// The hero crowd: shapes and colours straight from the app's face builder.
// Each face flies in, then drifts; positions and timings are the hf-* classes
// in global.css, because the site's CSP (style-src 'self') blocks style attributes.
const crowd = [
  ['squircle', '#f5a524', 'hf-1', 0], ['round', '#3b82f6', 'hf-2', 0.7], ['cloud', '#8b5cf6', 'hf-3', 2.8],
  ['hex', '#22a55b', 'hf-4', 1.4], ['drop', '#ec2f8a', 'hf-5', 2.1], ['tri', '#f97316', 'hf-6', 4.2],
] as const
---
<Base>
  <section class="hero relative mx-auto max-w-[1120px] px-5 pb-16 text-center sm:px-8">
    <div class="hero-crowd" aria-hidden="true">
      {crowd.map(([shape, color, position, delay]) => (
        <span class:list={['hero-face', position]}><span class="hero-face-in"><Face shape={shape} color={color} delay={delay} /></span></span>
      ))}
    </div>
    <h1 class="display relative mx-auto max-w-[18ch] text-[clamp(2.75rem,7.5vw,5rem)]">
      <span class="rise">Bots with faces,</span><br /><span class="rise rise-2">names, and a memory</span><br /><span class="rise rise-3">of their own.</span>
    </h1>
    <p class="lede rise rise-4 relative mx-auto mt-6">A handful of bots on your own Mac or Linux machine. Each keeps its own notes, uses the model you pick, and joins rooms with the people in your house.</p>
    <div class="rise rise-5 relative mt-8 flex flex-col items-center gap-4">
      <a class="button button-lg" href="/download/"><span data-download-label>Download for Mac</span></a>
      <a class="text-[15px] text-mute hover:text-accent" href={github}>Open source on GitHub</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-[1120px] px-5 sm:px-8">
    <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-[18px] border border-line">
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-0.5 border-b border-line px-5 py-3 text-[15px] sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between">
        <span class="flex items-center gap-2 font-semibold"><Face shape="squircle" color="#f5a524" size={22} />Kitchen</span>
        <span class="text-mute">A room with Scout, Ledger, and you</span>
      </div>
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-5 px-5 py-6 sm:px-8">
        <div class="flex justify-end">
          <div class="flex flex-col items-end gap-1">
            <span class="text-[13px] text-mute">You</span>
            <span class="bubble">@Scout what did we decide about the trip last month?</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
          <Face shape="round" color="#3b82f6" size={30} delay={1.2} />
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-1">
            <span class="text-[13px] text-mute">Scout</span>
            <span class="bubble">The second week of October, the cabin by the lake. Ledger has the deposit receipt from the 14th.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
          <Face shape="hex" color="#22a55b" size={30} delay={2.6} />
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-1">
            <span class="text-[13px] text-mute">Ledger</span>
            <span class="bubble">Deposit was 320 from the shared card. The balance is due two weeks before you leave.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="px-5 pb-5 sm:px-8">
        <div class="composer" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="composer-dot text-xl leading-none">+</span>
          <span class="flex-1 text-mute">Message Kitchen</span>
          <span class="composer-dot bg-ink text-paper"><svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="14" height="14" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M8 13V3M3.5 7.5 8 3l4.5 4.5"/></svg></span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-[40em] text-[15px] text-mute">Scout answered from the memory it kept of a chat four weeks earlier. Ledger joined because it was named. Neither one needed you to explain the trip again.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto grid max-w-[1120px] gap-10 px-5 pt-24 sm:px-8 lg:grid-cols-3 lg:gap-8">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
      <Face shape="round" color="#3b82f6" size={44} delay={0.4} />
      <h2 class="display-sm text-[1.6rem]">Memory that lasts</h2>
      <p class="max-w-[36em] text-mute">Every conversation stays until you archive it. Each bot has a soul, its own memory and a searchable history, and one About you text tells all your bots who you are. Overnight, bots dream over the day and keep what mattered.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
      <span class="flex"><Face shape="squircle" color="#f5a524" size={44} delay={1.1} /><span class="-ml-2.5"><Face shape="drop" color="#ec2f8a" size={44} delay={2.2} /></span></span>
      <h2 class="display-sm text-[1.6rem]">Rooms for people and bots</h2>
      <p class="max-w-[36em] text-mute">Put several bots and several people in one chat. Mention a bot to bring it in, or pick a main bot that answers when nobody is named. Bots can message each other, and you can watch the whole exchange.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
      <Face shape="hex" color="#22a55b" size={44} delay={1.8} />
      <h2 class="display-sm text-[1.6rem]">Runs where you say</h2>
      <p class="max-w-[36em] text-mute">The daemon lives on one machine and keeps working when the app is closed. Pair a phone or a second laptop with a short code on your network, over Tailscale, or through <a href="/docs/connect/">Hexbot Connect</a> when you are away.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto grid max-w-[1120px] gap-10 px-5 pt-24 sm:px-8 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,5fr)_minmax(0,7fr)] lg:gap-16">
    <h2 class="display-sm text-[clamp(2rem,4.5vw,2.75rem)]">Your data stays on your hardware.</h2>
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-5 text-[1.0625rem]">
      <p>Conversations, memory, files, and provider keys live in <code class="rounded-md bg-wash px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[.92em]">~/.hexbot</code> on the machine running the daemon. Bring your own API key or a subscription you already pay for.</p>
      <ul class="flex flex-col gap-3 border-t border-line pt-5">
        <li class="grid gap-1 sm:grid-cols-[12rem_1fr]"><strong class="font-semibold">Approvals</strong><span class="text-mute">Tools run only when you say so. Auto mode lets a small model wave through the low-risk ones.</span></li>
        <li class="grid gap-1 sm:grid-cols-[12rem_1fr]"><strong class="font-semibold">Devices you can revoke</strong><span class="text-mute">Every paired phone and laptop appears in settings with a revoke button.</span></li>
        <li class="grid gap-1 sm:grid-cols-[12rem_1fr]"><strong class="font-semibold">Delete means delete</strong><span class="text-mute">Removing a conversation also removes the memory a bot took from it.</span></li>
        <li class="grid gap-1 sm:grid-cols-[12rem_1fr]"><strong class="font-semibold">Connect stays out of the way</strong><span class="text-mute">Hexbot Connect brokers your identity and a hostname. Chat traffic never passes through it.</span></li>
        <li class="grid gap-1 sm:grid-cols-[12rem_1fr]"><strong class="font-semibold">Open source</strong><span class="text-mute">AGPL-3.0. Read it, fork it, run it yourself.</span></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-[720px] px-5 pt-28 text-center sm:px-8">
    <Logo tile size={88} class="mx-auto" />
    <h2 class="display-sm mt-6 text-[clamp(2rem,5vw,3rem)]">Get Hexbot.</h2>
    <p class="lede mx-auto mt-3">Free and open source, for Mac and Linux.</p>
    <div class="mt-7 flex flex-col items-center gap-3">
      <a class="button" href="/download/"><span data-download-label>Download for Mac</span></a>
      {downloads && (
        <details class="more w-full">
          <summary class="button button-quiet">More options<svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="14" height="14" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.75" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m4 6 4 4 4-4"/></svg></summary>
          <div class="mt-6 text-left"><DownloadList downloads={downloads} /></div>
          {downloads.channel === 'nightly' && <p class="mt-4 text-[15px] text-mute"><a class="text-ink underline decoration-line underline-offset-4 hover:text-accent" href="/download/#nightlies">Earlier nightly builds</a></p>}
        </details>
      )}
    </div>
  </section>
  <script src="../scripts/downloadButtons.ts"></script>
</Base>
